    "title": "Selecting Elements with jQuery",
    "cleanTitle": "Selecting Elements with jQuery",
    "category": "Selectors & Filters",
    "introduction": "Selectors form the heart of jQuery. This lesson covers 'Selecting Elements with jQuery' to query, filter, and isolate specific DOM nodes.",
    "learningObjective": "Learn how to accurately target matching elements using Selecting Elements with jQuery.",
    "prerequisites": "Lesson 021",
    "codeExample": "<!-- List container for testing selectors -->\n<div style=\"padding: 18px; background: #0f172a; border-radius: 10px; color: #e2e8f0;\">\n    <h4 style=\"color: #00e5d0; margin-top: 0;\">Testing: Selecting Elements with jQuery</h4>\n    <ul class=\"selector-list\" style=\"list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-bottom: 15px;\">\n        <li class=\"target-class\" style=\"padding: 8px 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; background: #1e293b; border-radius: 6px;\">Item 1 (Index 0)</li>\n        <li data-status=\"active\" style=\"padding: 8px 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; background: #1e293b; border-radius: 6px;\">Item 2 (Active Status)</li>\n        <li id=\"special-target\" style=\"padding: 8px 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; background: #1e293b; border-radius: 6px;\">Item 3 (#special-target)</li>\n        <li class=\"target-class\" style=\"padding: 8px 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; background: #1e293b; border-radius: 6px;\">Item 4 (Index 3)</li>\n    </ul>\n    <button id=\"btn-run-selector\" style=\"background: #00bfa5; color: #0b1120; border: none; padding: 8px 16px; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer;\">Apply Selecting Elements with jQuery</button>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n$('#btn-run-selector').on('click', function() {\n    $('.target-item').css({\n        'background': '#065f46',\n        'color': '#6ee7b7',\n        'border-left': '4px solid #00e5d0'\n    });\n});\n</script>",
    "expectedOutput": "Elements matching the selector criteria (Selecting Elements with jQuery) are highlighted with an emerald background and cyan border.",
    "resultExplanation": "Executes $('.target-item') and modifies matching collection items in a single chained call.",
    "notes": "Prefer ID selectors or class selectors for maximum DOM query performance.",
    "commonMistakes": "Omitting prefix symbols like '#' for IDs or '.' for classes in selector queries.",
    "securityNotes": "Never concatenate untrusted user input directly into selector strings.",
